J/A+A/537/A120      Rotational velocities of A-type stars. IV. (Zorec+, 2012)
================================================================================
Rotational velocities of A-type stars.
IV. Evolution of rotational velocities.
    Zorec J., Royer F.
   <Astron. Astrophys. 537, A120 (2012)>
   =2012A&A...537A.120Z
================================================================================
ADC_Keywords: Stars, A-type ; Stars, B-type ; Rotational velocities ;
              Stars, masses ; Stars, ages
Keywords: stars: early-type - stars: rotation - stars: evolution

Abstract:
    In previous works of this series, we have shown that late B- and early
    A-type stars have genuine bimodal distributions of rotational
    velocities and that late A-type stars lack slow rotators. The
    distributions of the surface angular velocity ratio Omega/Omega_crit_
    (Omega_crit_ is the critical angular velocity) have peculiar shapes
    according to spectral type groups, which can be caused by evolutionary
    properties.

    We aim to review the properties of these rotational velocity
    distributions in some detail as a function of stellar mass and age.

    We have gathered vsini for a sample of 2014 B6- to F2-type stars. We
    have determined the masses and ages for these objects with stellar
    evolution models. The (Teff,logL/L_{sun}_)-parameters were determined
    from the uvby-beta photometry and the HIPPARCOS parallaxes.

Description:
    Fundamental parameters for 2014 B6- to F2-type stars are presented.
    For each star, spectral type, effective temperature, luminosity, mass,
    age and projected rotational velocity are given, as well as remarks
    about their multiplicity and chemical peculiarity. The projected
    rotational velocities are taken from different sources and homogenized
    to the same scale.

